{"q":"504","t":"Base 7","d":"Easy","p":false,"c":"<p>Given an integer <code>num</code>, return <em>a string of its <strong>base 7</strong> representation</em>.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> num = 100\n<strong>Output:</strong> \"202\"\n</pre><p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> num = -7\n<strong>Output:</strong> \"-10\"\n</pre>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><code>-10<sup>7</sup> &lt;= num &lt;= 10<sup>7</sup></code></li>\n</ul>\n","h":[],"m":"{\r\n  \"name\": \"convertToBase7\",\r\n  \"params\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"name\": \"num\",\r\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"return\": {\r\n    \"type\": \"string\"\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n","g":[{"name":"Math","slug":"math"},{"name":"String","slug":"string"}],"s":[],"co":[["Microsoft","microsoft"],["Amazon","amazon"],["Google","google"],["Bloomberg","bloomberg"]],"cs":{"a":[],"b":[["Google","google",2]],"m":[["Amazon","amazon",10],["Microsoft","microsoft",5]]}}